(LST2-09 — an empty list prints exactly [].
 Also covers: LST2-10 (a nested list element renders recursively with its
 own brackets intact), LST2-11 (a map element, and a whole map, render as
 {"key": value, ...}).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-09.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   []
   [1, [2, 3], "four"]
   {"a": 1, "b": "two"}
   [{"a": 1, "b": "two"}, 9]
)
a list called blank is [].
print blank.
a list called nested is [1, [2, 3], "four"].
print nested.
a map called scores is {"a": 1, "b": "two"}.
print scores.
a list called holder is [scores, 9].
print holder.
